This solution uses a binary search-like algorithm to distribute the points across the possible values of the numbers. It also uses a strategy to guess the numbers based on the responses from Vasya, which allows Vitya to make up to 600 queries. Note that this is just one way to solve the problem, and there might be other more efficient ways.

To solve this problem, we need to determine if we can pave a set of paths such that each pasture has an odd number of paved paths, and if so, find the minimum possible length of the longest path in such a paving. We can solve this problem using a combination of prime factorization and suffix arrays.

